Backend Deployment Step 3

This document continues after the AWS EC2 instance launch. It records how the Ubuntu host was prepared, Docker and swap were configured, the DevOps repository was cloned, the backend image was built, MongoDB Atlas was secured, and the private backend container was verified.

> Security note: Never commit `.env`, database passwords, session secrets, email app passwords, or complete connection strings. Rotate all learning credentials before public deployment.

