## 6. Configure MongoDB Atlas

The Atlas deployment used:

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Project | `JerseyHub-DevOps` |
| Deployment | `jerseyhub-devops-db` |
| Tier | Free |
| Provider | AWS |
| Region | Sydney `ap-southeast-2` |
| Sample data | Disabled |

### Network access

Only the current EC2 public IPv4 address was added, using a `/32` entry.

Verify the EC2 outbound address with:

```bash
curl -4 https://checkip.amazonaws.com
```

If EC2 is stopped and started, its auto-assigned public address can change. Update the Atlas IP access-list entry when this happens.

### Database users

Two users were created:

| User | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `jerseyhub_setup_admin` | Initial Atlas setup administration |
| `jerseyhub_app` | Backend application access |

The application user was restricted to:

- Cluster: `jerseyhub-devops-db`
- Database: `jerseyhub`
- Role: `readWrite`

The backend must use `jerseyhub_app`, not the administrative account.

